  "version": 1,
  "note": "Tracked defaults for role-based model routing. The operator override lives in var/model_policy.json (editor-owned, never committed). Route order is authoritative: first enabled+allowed route wins. Provider catalogs change: run `newsroom models validate` to check ids against the live catalogs instead of trusting this file. V1.2-G2.4B: the `extract` role budget was raised to soft 200 / hard 300 logical requests per day. Measured demand on the frozen 24-Story sample was 159 semantic claim-equivalence decisions, which the previous hard cap of 50 truncated before Research quality could be measured. This is the ROLE budget only: route order, model choice, provider, the semantic prompt, the SAME_FACT rules and paid_enabled are unchanged. Shared-provider headroom check: the old note claimed extract(300) + judge(80) + utility(75) = 455 against gemini-3.5-flash-lite's 500/day quota and omitted `research`, which routes to the same model. The true figure was 505 against 500 - over-subscribed, and the check never actually held. `research` is back at 50: the cut to 40 rested on that false premise and is reverted so no arbitrary configuration is left behind. The real figure comes from the routing audit, not from summing budgets: only roles with a production call site consume the quota, and m4/review/evidence/v1_2_g2_4_model_routing_audit.json records `wired_in_production` and `wired_at` per role. Against that, judge(80) + extract(300) = 380 of gemini-3.5-flash-lite's 500/day, with 120 spare. `research` and `utility` are `wired_in_production: false` with no call sites - they are RESERVED, not dormant production roles, they consume nothing, and their budgets are placeholders rather than capacity. Budget arithmetic must therefore be read through the audit's wired roles only; summing this file's budgets overstates what the product can spend. `extract` and `judge` keep their budgets: both have gemini-3.1-flash-lite as a second 500 RPD route, so their real backing is 1000 across two models, not 500. daily_call_limit is the operator-declared per-model quota (Gemini AI Studio, per model, 2026-09-21: Flash-Lite 500 RPD, Flash 20 RPD); it is a local guardrail, and provider signals (429 quota) still win.",
